      "english": "The first expression means “the Necessary Existent.” As for maʿād, its linguistic meaning is returning; in the present theological discussion it signifies the soul's return to the body after its separation from it. This is an explanation of the particular theological use of the term, not a general dictionary claim that every occurrence of maʿād means bodily resurrection.",
