      "english": "The apparent assumption is that the governor of the coordinated expression is the same governor that acts on the first expression, operating through the coordinating particle; this is the majority position and is regarded here as sound. Others assign the grammatical operation directly to the coordinating particle, while yet others posit an implicit governor after it. A further view describes the coordinated word as governed by the word with which it is coordinated; arguments can be found for this account as well.\n\nOne might instead coordinate the disputed expression with “refinement” (taḥrīr), as reported from al-Dawwānī. The whole would then mean that the work represents the utmost refinement of discourse in bringing the intended objectives nearer—that is, arranging an argument so that the desired conclusion follows. The glossator finds that construction closer to the superficial wording but less fitting to the intended sense, and suggests that this is why the principal commentator does not examine it.",
